<item><title>Sierra Leone&apos;s vice presidency has produced no elected president</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-produced-no-elected-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-produced-no-elected-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A public policy analyst says the office has often served party balance rather than succession, and points to Solomon Berewa&apos;s 2007 defeat as evidence.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:19:02 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
